{{also|sage|Sage|saĝe|säge}}
==German==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmh|sage}}, from {{inh|de|goh|saga}}, from {{inh|de|gmw-pro|*sagu}}, from {{inh|de|gem-pro|*sagō}}, from {{der|de|ine-pro|*sek-||to cut}}.

Compare {{cog|nl|zaag}}, {{cog|fy|seage}}, {{cog|en|saw}}, {{cog|da|sav}}, {{cog|sv|såg}}; as well as (from {{cog|la|secāre}}) {{cog|it|sega}},  {{cog|fr|scie}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/ˈzɛːɡə/}} {{qualifier|standard; used naturally in western Germany and Switzerland}}
* {{IPA|de|/ˈzeːɡə/}} {{qualifier|overall more common; particularly northern and eastern regions}}
* {{audio|de|De-Säge.ogg|Audio}}
* {{hyphenation|de|Sä|ge}}

